  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening marine turtle conservation strategies in the Tartaruga Natural Reserve (Boa Vista, Cape Verde)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recipient will set up a field camp at Joao Barrosa Beach on the Island of Boa Vista and conduct daily patrols to protect nests and nesting females throughout the loggerhead nesting season as well as provide education outreach activities for local communities regarding marine turtle conservation. The USFWS will work closely with grantee in setting goals, priorities, and developing budgets, and will provide assistance as needed and requested in engaging with National Governmental and other institutions to improve collaboration and conservation outcomes. USFWS will also provide assistance as necessary to ensure effective collaboration and cooperation between all MTCA grant recipients working within Cape Verde.</narrative>
  </description>
